
Enable production ServiceLoader registration for
the existing TestNG lifecycle adapter.

Requirements:

1. Register the existing adapter through
   META-INF/services/org.testng.ITestNGListener
   in the TestNG integration module.

2. Reuse the existing no-argument constructor.

3. Ensure exactly one adapter instance owns
   lifecycle state per TestNG execution.

4. Do not register the adapter through @Listeners.

5. Prevent duplicate registration when another
   instance is registered programmatically.

6. Preserve the existing ROOT ownership and
   single-use lifecycle behavior.

7. Do not modify existing legacy listeners.

8. Do not migrate the configuration API yet.

9. Keep core independent of TestNG.

10. Do not introduce static singleton state.

Verification:

- Run normal Maven TestNG execution.
- Verify automatic discovery works.
- Verify one suite with multiple parallel tests.
- Verify correct context creation and cleanup.
- Verify no duplicate lifecycle callbacks.
- Verify no orphan contexts or configuration layers.
- Verify existing legacy listeners still execute.
- Run the complete TestNG module three times.

If global registration causes existing tests
to fail, investigate the exact interaction
before modifying tests or production behavior.

Do not weaken assertions or suppress failures.

Report exact test results and all compatibility
issues discovered.


